  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Income generating projects for women in southern Tolima, Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEUDES (Democratic Development Units Corporation) is a small flexible NGO based on a consortium of 18 social science professionals running a number of programmes with minimum infrastructure.  The basic premise is democracy, which means participatory management and a perspective of changing the grossly unequal distribution of power and wealth in Colombia.  In the present situation of conflict, CEUDES works with several of the civil society peace networks. A particular emphasis is support and training for women headed households.   

This project is based in southern Tolima working with indigenous women&#x2019;s groups to improve the agricultural practices of the community through training in sustainable organic farming techniques and distribution of materials.</narrative>
  </description>
